# Generic robot-skill action. One action type fronts every high-level skill
# (pick, place, home, ...) so new skills add NO new message and NO rebuild of
# manipulation_msgs. The skill is selected by name; its arguments travel as a
# JSON object string. Each skill declares its own param schema in the skill
# registry (manipulation_policy/skills); the skill_server validates against it.

# --- Goal ---
string skill             # registered skill name, e.g. "pick", "place", "home"
string params_json       # JSON object of skill arguments, e.g. {"object":"bread"}
---
# --- Result ---
bool success             # skill completed without abort
string message           # human-readable outcome / failure reason
string result_json       # JSON object of skill-specific outputs (may be "{}")
---
# --- Feedback ---
string state             # current skill phase / state machine label
float32 progress         # 0.0..1.0 best-effort progress (0 if unknown)
